<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Off-Scan: Set Mode to No Mode, clear Readies]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this device is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Settings, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Rdy_OSet);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan - usual analog fanout functions are performed]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Fanout :  PROCESS -- ANALOG FAN OUT
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Uses P_Mode V3.0. Added Inf_Lib. Changed
default configuration to Split-Range (cool / heat); added Cfg_HasNav
bits, Cfg_NavTag strings for navigation to connected obects.
V3.0-01  2014-01-22:  Corrected Parameter Descriptions only.
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Modified to use P_Mode V3.1.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, but using P_Mode V3.1-01.
============================================================
This Instruction fans one (primary) analog output signal out
to multiple (secondary) users.  It provides:

*  Input for target CV from Primary in Engineering Units
*  Ramping of Output CV to target at specified Rate of Change (EU/sec)
*  Calculation of up to 8 secondary CVs, each with its own ratio (slope)
and offset (intercept) from the Primary.
*  Selection of ratio and offset from Configuration (maintenance faceplate only) or
from Settings (operator or program, with mode selection) for each signal.
*  Program and Operator Modes for entry of selected ratios and offsets.
*  Initialization of the Primary when ALL secondaries request initialization,
using a configured initialization value, or using CV1
(the high priority secondary) initialization value.
(This back-calculation accounts for the CV1 ratio and offset.)

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)[CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag) LOWER(Cfg_CV1_Label,Cfg_CV1_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV2_Label,Cfg_CV2_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV3_Label,Cfg_CV3_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV4_Label,Cfg_CV4_EU) ,LOWER(Cfg_CV5_Label,Cfg_CV5_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV6_Label,Cfg_CV6_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV7_Label,Cfg_CV7_EU) LOWER(Cfg_CV8_Label,Cfg_CV8_EU) ,CONCAT(Cfg_CVNavTag,Cfg_NavTag[0],Cfg_NavTag[1]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[2],Cfg_NavTag[3]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[4],Cfg_NavTag[5]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[6],Cfg_NavTag[7]) CONCAT(Cfg_CV_EU,Inf_Lib,Inf_Type) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.

This object does NOT have the following Modes:
Hand
Override]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)OTU(Mode.Inp_Hand)OTU(Mode.Inp_Ovrd)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================

These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the maximum allowed value for the Rate of Change Configuration (Cfg_CVRoCLim) (in EU/sec)

If the rate is negative, infinite or not a number, no valid Rate of Change can be entered.  Set the maximum to zero.
This will force the CV Rate of Change to zero, which does NO ramping/limiting.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_MaxCVRoC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs check that each output CV's configured "Takeup" (bias mop-up) Rate is valid.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV1TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV1TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV1TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV2TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV2TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV2TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV3TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV3TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV3TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV4TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV4TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV4TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV5TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV5TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV5TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV6TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV6TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV6TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV7TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV7TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV7TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_CV8TakeupRate,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_CV8TakeupRate,3.40282347E38) ]CLR(Cfg_CV8TakeupRate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV1 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV1 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV1Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn1,(Cfg_CV1Min-Cfg_CV1Offset)/Cfg_CV1Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn1,(Cfg_CV1Max-Cfg_CV1Offset)/Cfg_CV1Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV1Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV1Min,Val_MinCVIn1) MOV(Cfg_CV1Max,Val_MaxCVIn1) ,LES(Cfg_CV1Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn1,(Cfg_CV1Max-Cfg_CV1Offset)/Cfg_CV1Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn1,(Cfg_CV1Min-Cfg_CV1Offset)/Cfg_CV1Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn1) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn1) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn1) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV2 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV2 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV2Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn2,(Cfg_CV2Min-Cfg_CV2Offset)/Cfg_CV2Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn2,(Cfg_CV2Max-Cfg_CV2Offset)/Cfg_CV2Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV2Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV2Min,Val_MinCVIn2) MOV(Cfg_CV2Max,Val_MaxCVIn2) ,LES(Cfg_CV2Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn2,(Cfg_CV2Max-Cfg_CV2Offset)/Cfg_CV2Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn2,(Cfg_CV2Min-Cfg_CV2Offset)/Cfg_CV2Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn2) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn2) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn2) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV3 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV3 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV3Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn3,(Cfg_CV3Min-Cfg_CV3Offset)/Cfg_CV3Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn3,(Cfg_CV3Max-Cfg_CV3Offset)/Cfg_CV3Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV3Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV3Min,Val_MinCVIn3) MOV(Cfg_CV3Max,Val_MaxCVIn3) ,LES(Cfg_CV3Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn3,(Cfg_CV3Max-Cfg_CV3Offset)/Cfg_CV3Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn3,(Cfg_CV3Min-Cfg_CV3Offset)/Cfg_CV3Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn3) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn3) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn3) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV4 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV4 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV4Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn4,(Cfg_CV4Min-Cfg_CV4Offset)/Cfg_CV4Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn4,(Cfg_CV4Max-Cfg_CV4Offset)/Cfg_CV4Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV4Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV4Min,Val_MinCVIn4) MOV(Cfg_CV4Max,Val_MaxCVIn4) ,LES(Cfg_CV4Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn4,(Cfg_CV4Max-Cfg_CV4Offset)/Cfg_CV4Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn4,(Cfg_CV4Min-Cfg_CV4Offset)/Cfg_CV4Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn4) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn4) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn4) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV5 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV5 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV5Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn5,(Cfg_CV5Min-Cfg_CV5Offset)/Cfg_CV5Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn5,(Cfg_CV5Max-Cfg_CV5Offset)/Cfg_CV5Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV5Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV5Min,Val_MinCVIn5) MOV(Cfg_CV5Max,Val_MaxCVIn5) ,LES(Cfg_CV5Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn5,(Cfg_CV5Max-Cfg_CV5Offset)/Cfg_CV5Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn5,(Cfg_CV5Min-Cfg_CV5Offset)/Cfg_CV5Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn5) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn5) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn5) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV6 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV6 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV6Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn6,(Cfg_CV6Min-Cfg_CV6Offset)/Cfg_CV6Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn6,(Cfg_CV6Max-Cfg_CV6Offset)/Cfg_CV6Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV6Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV6Min,Val_MinCVIn6) MOV(Cfg_CV6Max,Val_MaxCVIn6) ,LES(Cfg_CV6Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn6,(Cfg_CV6Max-Cfg_CV6Offset)/Cfg_CV6Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn6,(Cfg_CV6Min-Cfg_CV6Offset)/Cfg_CV6Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn6) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn6) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn6) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV7 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV7 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV7Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn7,(Cfg_CV7Min-Cfg_CV7Offset)/Cfg_CV7Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn7,(Cfg_CV7Max-Cfg_CV7Offset)/Cfg_CV7Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV7Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV7Min,Val_MinCVIn7) MOV(Cfg_CV7Max,Val_MaxCVIn7) ,LES(Cfg_CV7Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn7,(Cfg_CV7Max-Cfg_CV7Offset)/Cfg_CV7Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn7,(Cfg_CV7Min-Cfg_CV7Offset)/Cfg_CV7Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn7) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn7) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn7) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn7) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These values are computed to assist the HMI in drawing the
graphs of the functions on the Operator Faceplate.

CV8 Minimum (left-most point on X axis) and CV8 Maximum (right-most point on X axis)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_CV8Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn8,(Cfg_CV8Min-Cfg_CV8Offset)/Cfg_CV8Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn8,(Cfg_CV8Max-Cfg_CV8Offset)/Cfg_CV8Ratio) ,EQU(Cfg_CV8Ratio,0.0) MOV(Cfg_CV8Min,Val_MinCVIn8) MOV(Cfg_CV8Max,Val_MaxCVIn8) ,LES(Cfg_CV8Ratio,0.0) CPT(Val_MinCVIn8,(Cfg_CV8Max-Cfg_CV8Offset)/Cfg_CV8Ratio) CPT(Val_MaxCVIn8,(Cfg_CV8Min-Cfg_CV8Offset)/Cfg_CV8Ratio) ][GRT(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn8) MOV(Val_CVEUMin,Val_MinCVIn8) ,LES(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn8) MOV(Val_CVEUMax,Val_MaxCVIn8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung checks that the configured Maxima and Minima are valid
and flags an Err_ bit for any that are not.

Scale ranges cannot have the same max and min (but they can be reversed).

Clamping max cannot be less than clamping min.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Cfg_CVEUMax,Cfg_CVEUMin) OTE(Err_EU) ,LES(Cfg_CVMax,Cfg_CVMin) OTE(Err_Limit) ,LES(Cfg_CV1Max,Cfg_CV1Min) OTE(Err_CV1Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV2) LES(Cfg_CV2Max,Cfg_CV2Min) OTE(Err_CV2Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV3) LES(Cfg_CV3Max,Cfg_CV3Min) OTE(Err_CV3Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV4) LES(Cfg_CV4Max,Cfg_CV4Min) OTE(Err_CV4Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV5) LES(Cfg_CV5Max,Cfg_CV5Min) OTE(Err_CV5Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV6) LES(Cfg_CV6Max,Cfg_CV6Min) OTE(Err_CV6Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV7) LES(Cfg_CV7Max,Cfg_CV7Min) OTE(Err_CV7Limit) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV8) LES(Cfg_CV8Max,Cfg_CV8Min) OTE(Err_CV8Limit) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SETTINGS PROCESSING
============================================================
These rung handle received Settings:

Always limit the entered Rate of Change Limit to be between 0.0 and the configured Maximum.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(PSet_CVRoCLim,Cfg_MaxCVRoC) NEQ(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,0.0) MOV(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,PSet_CVRoCLim) ,LES(PSet_CVRoCLim,0.0) CLR(PSet_CVRoCLim) ,GRT(OSet_CVRoCLim,Cfg_MaxCVRoC) NEQ(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,0.0) MOV(Cfg_MaxCVRoC,OSet_CVRoCLim) ,LES(OSet_CVRoCLim,0.0) CLR(OSet_CVRoCLim) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Program Mode,
copy the Program Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog)MOV(PSet_CVRoCLim,Val_CVRoCLim);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Program Mode,
copy the Program Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog)[[XIC(Cfg_CV1RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV1Ratio,Val_CV1Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV1OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV1Offset,Val_CV1Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV2) [XIC(Cfg_CV2RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV2Ratio,Val_CV2Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV2OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV2Offset,Val_CV2Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV3) [XIC(Cfg_CV3RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV3Ratio,Val_CV3Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV3OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV3Offset,Val_CV3Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV4) [XIC(Cfg_CV4RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV4Ratio,Val_CV4Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV4OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV4Offset,Val_CV4Offset) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Program Mode,
copy the Program Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog)[XIC(Cfg_HasCV5) [XIC(Cfg_CV5RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV5Ratio,Val_CV5Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV5OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV5Offset,Val_CV5Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV6) [XIC(Cfg_CV6RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV6Ratio,Val_CV6Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV6OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV6Offset,Val_CV6Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV7) [XIC(Cfg_CV7RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV7Ratio,Val_CV7Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV7OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV7Offset,Val_CV7Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV8) [XIC(Cfg_CV8RatioSrc) MOV(PSet_CV8Ratio,Val_CV8Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV8OffsetSrc) MOV(PSet_CV8Offset,Val_CV8Offset) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Operator or Maintenance Mode,
copy the Operator Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ]MOV(OSet_CVRoCLim,Val_CVRoCLim);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Operator or Maintenance Mode,
copy the Operator Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ][[XIC(Cfg_CV1RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV1Ratio,Val_CV1Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV1OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV1Offset,Val_CV1Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV2) [XIC(Cfg_CV2RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV2Ratio,Val_CV2Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV2OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV2Offset,Val_CV2Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV3) [XIC(Cfg_CV3RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV3Ratio,Val_CV3Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV3OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV3Offset,Val_CV3Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV4) [XIC(Cfg_CV4RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV4Ratio,Val_CV4Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV4OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV4Offset,Val_CV4Offset) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Operator or Maintenance Mode,
copy the Operator Settings to the acutally-used Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ][XIC(Cfg_HasCV5) [XIC(Cfg_CV5RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV5Ratio,Val_CV5Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV5OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV5Offset,Val_CV5Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV6) [XIC(Cfg_CV6RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV6Ratio,Val_CV6Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV6OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV6Offset,Val_CV6Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV7) [XIC(Cfg_CV7RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV7Ratio,Val_CV7Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV7OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV7Offset,Val_CV7Offset) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasCV8) [XIC(Cfg_CV8RatioSrc) MOV(OSet_CV8Ratio,Val_CV8Ratio) ,XIC(Cfg_CV8OffsetSrc) MOV(OSet_CV8Offset,Val_CV8Offset) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the CV1 Ratio is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Ratio value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_CV1RatioSrc)MOV(Cfg_CV1Ratio,Val_CV1Ratio);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the CV1 Offset is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Offset value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_CV1OffsetSrc)MOV(Cfg_CV1Offset,Val_CV1Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV2 is not used, or if its Ratio is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Ratio value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV2) ,XIO(Cfg_CV2RatioSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV2Ratio,Val_CV2Ratio);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV2 is not used, or if its Offset is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Offset value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV2) ,XIO(Cfg_CV2OffsetSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV2Offset,Val_CV2Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV3 is not used, or if its Ratio is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Ratio value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV3) ,XIO(Cfg_CV3RatioSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV3Ratio,Val_CV3Ratio);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV3 is not used, or if its Offset is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Offset value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV3) ,XIO(Cfg_CV3OffsetSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV3Offset,Val_CV3Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV4 is not used, or if its Ratio is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Ratio value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV4) ,XIO(Cfg_CV4RatioSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV4Ratio,Val_CV4Ratio);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV4 is not used, or if its Offset is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Offset value using the Configuration instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasCV4) ,XIO(Cfg_CV4OffsetSrc) ]MOV(Cfg_CV4Offset,Val_CV4Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If CV5 is not used, or if its Ratio is not configured to use Operator/Program
Settings, set its Ratio value using the Configuration instead.]]>
